      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good, this closes the coverage gaps and the InvalidArgument handler returning the specific message is the right call.\n\nOne caution: @flask_app.errorhandler(ValueError) / (TypeError) are app-wide. A genuine server-side bug that happens to raise ValueError or TypeError (not client input, e.g. something in a plugin or config read) now comes back as a 400 \u0027Invalid request\u0027 with no stack trace. Flask only auto-logs unhandled exceptions; once a handler catches it, that log goes away, so real 500s get hidden as client errors. Consider logging the exception here (logger.exception(ex)) or narrowing the catch so genuine 500s stay visible.",
